The flaw is tracked as CVE-2026-47100 and rated 8.7 in CVSS 4.0 ([Sansec, 2026-05-14](https://sansec.io/research/funnelkit-woocommerce-vulnerability-exploited); [ENISA EUVD-2026-30936](https://euvd.enisa.europa.eu/enisa/eu_vulnerability_database/EUVD-2026-30936)). The 40,000+ figure is the number of stores using the plugin, not of exploited stores: Sansec found the fake Google Tag Manager loader in at least one case ([Sansec, 2026-05-14](https://sansec.io/research/funnelkit-woocommerce-vulnerability-exploited)), and FunnelKit later said that of more than 1,300 sites it monitored in the nine days after disclosure, three showed signs of compromise before its mitigations took effect, and that the exploitation path had been closed after the fix was pushed to older branches through WordPress.org automatic updates ([The Hacker News, updated 2026-05-31](https://thehackernews.com/2026/05/funnel-builder-flaw-under-active.html)). The skimmer is tailored to each store and streamed over a WebSocket that the loader opens in the shopper's browser; no source describes WebSocket connections from the WordPress PHP process or exposure of Swiss or EU public portals, and the check FunnelKit advises is a review of the plugin's External Scripts setting ([Sansec, 2026-05-14](https://sansec.io/research/funnelkit-woocommerce-vulnerability-exploited)).
